    </example>
    <example>
        <introduction>
            <p>
              For each of the scenarios presented explain the meaning of the given expression in terms of the stated scenario.    
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Suppose that <m>h(t)</m> represents the height of a ball, in feet, <m>t</m> seconds after it has been thrown.
                    Explain the meaning of the statement: <m>h(3)=4.35</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                   Suppose that <m>W(a)</m> represents the weight of a dog, in pounds, at an age of <m>a</m> weeks.
                   Explain the meaning of the statement: <m>W(6)=28</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.5in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Suppose that <m>S(t)</m> represents the number of US states, <m>t</m> years after 1776. 
                    Explain the meaning of the statement: <m>S(30)=17</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </example>
    <example>
        <introduction>
            <p>
               Resident students taking between 6 and 12 credit hours at a local community college paid $382.50 per credit hour for tuition, $30 per semester for a student records fee, and $15 per semester for a technology fee.  Let <m>f(c)</m>  be the total one-semester cost (in dollars) of tuition and fees for a student who is taking <m>c</m> credit hours. 
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                  What is the slope of the graph of <m>f</m> ?  What does it mean in this situation?  
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                 Find an equation for <m>f</m>.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                  Find <m>f(9)</m>.  What does it mean in this situation? 
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                  Find <m>c</m> when <m>f(c)=1200</m>.  What does it mean in this situation? 
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    What is the domain of <m>f(c)</m>?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </example>
</worksheet>